  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. The gap holds; the registry names and the overlap with two open items drifted.\nCODE: scala.py binds var_types only from function params (_extract_param_types_scala, scala.py ~1363), val_definition through _declared_type_name (annotation or new; ~1374-1387) and class_parameter (~1392). scala.py never populates FileAnalysis.method_return_types and never reads self._method_return_type_registry (grep: 0 hits). No scala commit since 09-10 adds inference (git log: INV-vokut fdd99a9eae, WI-kilap d5f8060a45, WI-tipoh, INV-midag -- adjacent, not this).\nREPRO (scratch fixture, survey, fresh cache): object A { def mk(): FileWriter; val x = mk(); x.write; val y: FileWriter = mk(); y.flush; for (z <- xs) z.close; xs.foreach(w => w.append(..)); mk().getEncoding }\n  y.flush -> scala:java.io.FileWriter:0-0:flush (typed; annotation control)\n  x.write / z.close / w.append / mk().getEncoding -> scala:external:0-0:<m>, receiver_type_hint None. All four named shapes reproduce.\nNAME DRIFT: there is no _objc_return_type_registry or swift_return_type_registry. objc: method_return_type_registry parameter of _extract_edges (objc.py ~1540, library rows ~1332); swift: populates analysis.method_return_types (swift.py ~692) into the BASE registry, base.py ~4446-4458 (self._method_return_type_registry, library_signatures merged). Since scala already subclasses TreeSitterAnalyzer, the base half is built; scala needs Pass-1 population + a Pass-2 read. There is no library_signatures/scala.yaml.\nOVERLAP (surface, not fold): WI-hijot (P4 todo_soft someday, 'INV-dihos Phase 3: Return-Type Registry for Scala') prescribes exactly the call-result/chained half of this item; WI-jubim (P3) is the library-row half (Runtime.getRuntime().exec in scala/kotlin). This item adds for-binder and lambda parameter, which neither names.\nNOT RE-MEASURED: the sbt 23.43% / lila 8.02% hinted shares and the 15,872 / 38,008 external method edges (would need two large corpus runs).\nPROPOSAL: record WI-hijot and WI-jubim as related (or fold WI-hijot into this, owner's call); fix the two registry names in the description."  # 342f
